 "question": "Which stored fields carry the hit-quality factor (0.75 to 2) of L3323 and the extra factor 2 on mobile anti-air rounds of L3322?",
 "sourceFacts": {
  "method": "This records the end of the source-only search for the two untraced factors. Every numeric field of the projectile object of 24 weapon and mine files was listed and compared between the weapons that fit the L3323 rule and the three mobile anti-air rounds that are twice the rule. Field_58d24a64 is 0.75 in all 24 projectile objects, equal to the low end of EA's tank ranges. It never varies, so no weapon can show whether changing it changes the low figure. Field_7fa53094 is 2 in every material-grid cell read with a non-zero damage value (tank, helicopter and jet targets, both grids where read), equal to the high end of EA's tank ranges. It never varies either, and aircraft cells hold the same 2 although aircraft figures show no range. Field_84b71f89 is 1 in the three mobile anti-air rounds and 2 in every other projectile of the same class. It is the only stored difference found that lines up with the anti-air figures being twice the rule. No registry row names it. Field_be8c8762 (2, 5 or 6) and Field_c30df0ef (35 to 5000) vary but do not line up with either factor. The registry rows of the anti-air rounds (damage, falloff, speed, gravity, drag, lifetime, DamageMultiplier 1) hold no 2. The stored angle curves of L3201 (side 1 to 1.9, front up to 1.1, rear 3.2) do not give 0.75 to 2. Game code is not in the saved data, so which field the game reads cannot be seen.",
